{
  "schema": "phx.skills.checks.v1",
  "spec": "SPEC-V2-2216",
  "pack": "packs/study-duties",
  "walk": [
    "contract",
    "readings",
    "leeches",
    "assessment",
    "feedback",
    "integrity",
    "compose"
  ],
  "paths": [
    "skills/packs/study-duties/*",
    "scripts/study-duties-probe.py",
    "scripts/persona-core-probe.py",
    "skills/packs/persona-core/*",
    "skills/packs/*/examples/*",
    "scripts/law-professors-probe.py",
    "scripts/language-mentors-probe.py",
    "scripts/lsat-coach-probe.py",
    "scripts/learning-science-probe.py"
  ],
  "note": "SPEC-V2-2216. Tree rows run from the skills directory against any --root. The first fourteen run study-duties-probe.py's classes over every persona output in the tree: the duty templates and x- declarations, the law reading band and its scaling, the leech doctor's contrast, one keyed answer and every choice explained (lsat-coach's multiple-choice format, adopted), specific feedback, no placeholder and one conversational turn. The compose stage calls the classes the duty composes with and never copies them: learning-science's general pedagogy, law-professors' citations, language-mentors' CEFR ratio, glosses and focus, and lsat-coach's choice explanations. Advisory rows report and never refuse.",
